<%# THE ERROR PAGE ("Oh No!"), shared by static/error and static/access_denied
    so a refusal and a missing record are one page, not two copies. The words
    are the operator's, verbatim (2026-10-10): a signed-out viewer met a bare
    "Error" heading top-left, and the page now walks them through why they
    might be here, in the order they would check.

    The page's own error is the yielded block, shown under the walk-through,
    small: a specific sentence ("That record was not found.", a refusal's own
    remedy) beats a generic one whenever the site has it.

    The picture is a contest's to fill (operator, 2026-10-10). Its square is
    sized before anything loads, so a picture arriving late, or never, moves
    nothing (standing rule: no element pushes others out of place); one
    config value, Danbooru.config.error_page_image_url, drops the winner in. %>
<div class="oh-no">
  <h1 class="oh-no-title">Oh No!</h1>

  <%# The placeholder is always drawn, and the picture laid over it (review,
      2026-10-10): while the picture loads the square shows the placeholder,
      not a page-coloured gap; a picture that fails hides itself instead of
      drawing the browser's broken-image symbol; a loaded one marks the
      square so the placeholder's dashes do not show in its letterbox. %>
  <div class="oh-no-art">
    <div class="oh-no-art-placeholder" aria-hidden="true">
      <%= image_icon(class: "oh-no-art-placeholder-icon") %>
    </div>
    <% if Danbooru.config.error_page_image_url.present? %>
      <%= tag.img src: Danbooru.config.error_page_image_url, alt: Danbooru.config.error_page_image_alt, class: "oh-no-art-image", decoding: "async",
                  onload: "this.parentNode.classList.add('is-loaded')", onerror: "this.hidden = true" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <p class="oh-no-intro">You have reached the error page.  Which error, we cannot say for sure, because that's just the way computers work.  The following flowchart of conditionals may help:</p>

  <%# A flowchart of conditionals: each step is reached by answering "yes,
      and still here" to the one above it, so the steps are numbered nodes on
      one rail rather than a loose list of tips. role="list" because
      Safari/VoiceOver drops the list semantics of a list styled
      list-style: none, and the order is the point (review, 2026-10-10).

      Each step is a <details> toggle, collapsed by default (operator,
      2026-10-10): closed, the page reads as the flowchart's questions alone,
      and the reader opens the one that fits. The green triangle on the
      right says a step opens; it points down while it is open. Native
      <details>, so it needs no script and opens from the keyboard. %>
  <ol class="oh-no-flow" role="list">
    <li class="oh-no-step">
      <details class="oh-no-toggle">
        <summary>
          <h2 class="oh-no-question">Have you registered?</h2>
          <span class="oh-no-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="oh-no-answer">
          <p>The majority of this site is only available to registered viewers.</p>
          <p>You may register by clicking <span class="oh-no-ui">"Manage Session"</span>, <span class="oh-no-ui">"Booru: Log In"</span> and then <span class="oh-no-ui">"Create Account"</span>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>

    <li class="oh-no-step">
      <details class="oh-no-toggle">
        <summary>
          <h2 class="oh-no-question">Are you already registered, but still here?</h2>
          <span class="oh-no-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="oh-no-answer">
          <p>Your login token may be stale.  Click the <span class="oh-no-ui">"Manage Session"</span> button and check your logins for any amber or red lamps.  If so, follow the instructions on the panel.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>

    <li class="oh-no-step">
      <details class="oh-no-toggle">
        <summary>
          <h2 class="oh-no-question">Registered, logged in with fresh tokens, and yet, here you are again?</h2>
          <span class="oh-no-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="oh-no-answer">
          <%# The bin is the header's own purge icon (IconHelper#purge_icon), not a
              button: the working one is in the corner, and the sentence says so. %>
          <p>Try performing a full purge of site data by clicking the <span class="oh-no-bin" role="img" aria-label="junk bin icon"><%= purge_icon %></span> in the upper right corner.  This will log you out of the services, purge your cache of all site data (with only a few exceptions) and give you a fresh start.  Try logging in again.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>

    <li class="oh-no-step">
      <details class="oh-no-toggle">
        <summary>
          <h2 class="oh-no-question">Registered, newly logged in with a brand new set of tokens, and this page keeps popping up?</h2>
          <span class="oh-no-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="oh-no-answer">
          <p>It's possible this surface is not intended to be available to your user level--or at all.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>

    <li class="oh-no-step">
      <details class="oh-no-toggle">
        <summary>
          <h2 class="oh-no-question">So you're registered, session tokens fresh out the box, and absolutely sure something is supposed to be here?</h2>
          <span class="oh-no-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="oh-no-answer">
          <p>You may report the bug to <span class="oh-no-ui">@Fourier:41chan.net</span> in the appropriate channel under <span class="oh-no-ui">"get help"</span> in the 41chan Matrix Homeserver.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="oh-no-details">
    <%= yield %>
  </div>
</div>
